// Detection: DC01's own machine account ($ account) authenticates via
// NTLM to a workstation - a domain controller has no legitimate reason to
// log on TO a workstation this way. This is the relayed-coercion signature.
// ATT&CK: T1557.001 Adversary-in-the-Middle (relay half), T1187 Forced Authentication
// Data source: SecurityEvent Event ID 4624 (Logon) type 3 (Network) on WS01
// Severity: Critical
// Known false positives: essentially none in a correctly functioning
// environment - a DC machine account authenticating outbound to a
// workstation is anomalous by construction, which is exactly why this is
// one of the stronger signals in the whole project.

SecurityEvent
| where Computer has "WS01"
| where EventID == 4624
| where LogonType == 3
| where AuthenticationPackageName == "NTLM"
| where TargetUserName endswith "$" // machine account
| where TargetUserName has "DC01"
| project TimeGenerated, Computer, TargetUserName, IpAddress, LogonType, AuthenticationPackageName
| order by TimeGenerated desc
